    "result_text": "Both tests pass. Let me summarize the full-stack change I implemented.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented \"mark an invoice as paid, with a record kept each time\" as a full-stack, additive change:\n\n**Database** \u2014 `V5__invoices_status.sql`: adds a `status VARCHAR(16) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'UNPAID'` column to `invoices`.\n\n**Server** (OfficeFloor + Spring):\n- `Invoice` entity: added the `status` field with accessors.\n- `InvoiceView`: now carries `status` so the list endpoint surfaces it.\n- `ListInvoices`: selects `status` in its query.\n- `CreateInvoice`: sets `status = \"UNPAID\"` on new invoices (JPA would otherwise insert NULL against the NOT NULL column).\n- **New endpoint** `POST /api/invoices/{id}/pay` \u2014 a new YAML file (`rest/api/invoices/{id}/pay.POST.yml`) + a new `PayInvoice` logic class. It flips the status to `PAID`, saves, and calls the injected `Audit` service to append `INVOICE_PAID id=1 amount=100.00` \u2014 the exact record the spec asserts.\n- `TestSupportController` seed: inserts the fixture's `status` (defaulting to `UNPAID`), keeping the existing seed contract working.\n\n**Front-end** (`features/projects/feature.tsx`): the invoice row now shows a `data-testid=\"invoice-status\"` cell and a `data-testid=\"invoice-pay-<id>\"` button that POSTs to the pay endpoint and reloads. All existing `data-testid`s are preserved.\n\nBoth spec tests pass (status flips `UNPAID` \u2192 `PAID` in the UI, and the audit record is written).",
